 Wrap every container boot in Qvolution-work/dashboard/qv-slot guest. Use `qv-slot perf` ONLY for a short timing-measurement step (it holds two build slots and blocks the fleet's builds); never for whole suites or app runs. Use run_in_background for long
 runs and wait for the notification.
 
+Guest slots default `DARLING_ISOLATED_HOME=1`. Use a fresh prefix with a runtime containing
+host-folder-isolation; it creates real home folders and refuses existing host symlinks.
+For an explicit normal-behavior control set `DARLING_ISOLATED_HOME=0` on that command.
+The option takes effect when darlingserver starts; stop a prefix before changing modes.
+Keep the qv-host-guard snapshot/verify around every run, including shutdown and failures.
+`DARLING_APP_CONTAINER=1` remains Catalyst's separate per-app CoreFoundation option.
 
